          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Entry into Politics</strong><br>\nFrançois Mitterrand served as an officer in the French army during World War II and was imprisoned by the Germans. After the war, he quickly rose in politics, holding various ministerial positions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Opposition and Political Ascent</strong><br>\nBefore becoming president, Mitterrand led the opposition against de Gaulle's Fifth Republic, criticizing its concentration of presidential power. He unsuccessfully ran for president twice before finally winning in 1981.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Socialism and Reforms</strong><br>\nAs the first socialist president of the Fifth Republic, Mitterrand implemented extensive reforms, including the nationalization of major industries and banks, the increase in social welfare benefits, and the establishment of the 39-hour work week.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
